struction in a predoctoral lab course. Moderation of literature reviews and other seminars as needed. Participation in the development of clinical assessments and standards. Clinical supervision of dental students and residents involved in patient care. Adherence with faculty calibration standards and the best practices guidelines of the AAPD. CLINICAL CARE: Maintain existing board certification and any hospital privileges. Optional participation in College of Dentistry committees and priorities. Individuals new to academics will be expected to participate in professional development activities to establish a scholarly foundation for didactic and clinical teaching activities Additional duties at the discretion of the department chair. Oversee students in clinical settings, ensuring competency in patient-centered care. Provide mentorship and guidance to junior faculty and residents. SERVICE: Optional participation in College of Dentistry committees and priorities. Individuals new to academics will be expected to participate in professional development activities to establish a scholarly foundation for didactic and clinical teaching activities Additional duties at the discretion of the department chair. Oversee students in clinical settings, ensuring competency in patient-centered care. Provide mentorship and guidance to junior faculty and residents. SUPERVISORY Oversee students in clinical settings, ensuring competency in patient-centered care. Provide mentorship and guidance to junior faculty and residents."
