th science colleges -- Medicine, Dentistry, Pharmacy, Nursing, Graduate Health Sciences, and Health Professions. UT Health Sciences spans the state with its four major, regional clinical health science locations in Memphis, Knoxville, Chattanooga, and Nashville, as well as more than 100 clinical education sites across Tennessee. UT Health Sciences is the largest educator of health care professionals in the state and operates the state’s largest residency and fellowship advanced training programs. Located in West Tennessee on the banks of the Mississippi River, Memphis is the second-largest city in the state and among the largest cities in the Southeast. The Greater Memphis metropolitan area has more than 1.3 million residents, and the city ranks among those with the lowest cost of living in the country. It is home to a vibrant restaurant scene, a revitalized Downtown, the Midtown Arts District, many scenic neighborhoods, an active medical district, and a burgeoning airport in the midst of a $214 million modernization. Memphis boasts attractions, including Elvis Presley’s Graceland, the Memphis Grizzlies, historic Beale Street, the National Civil Rights Museum, the second-largest urban county park in the United States, and the Memphis in May World Championship Barbecue Cooking Contest. Responsibilities include providing didactic and clinical instruction to dental hygiene students. Supervise and mentor students during patient care, ensuring the highest standard of clinical practice and safety. Participate in curriculum development, assessment, and continuous improvement initiatives within the department. Engage in scholarly activities, including research, presentations, and publications as appropriate. Participate in departmental, college, and university committees and meetings as assigned. Contribute to community outreach, continuing education, and public service programs aligned with the department’s mission. Maintain compliance with all accreditation standards and 