    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/9325": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Health Informatics and Information Management (HIIM)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Memphis, TN, United States The University of Tennessee Health Sciences invites applications and nominations for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor in the Health Informatics and Information Management (HIIM) program. This is a twelve-month faculty appointment in the fully online Master of Health Informatics and Information Management program. Faculty members also contribute to the education and mentorship of doctoral students in the Health Outcomes and Policy Research Program's Health Informatics and Information Management concentration. The University of Tennessee Health Sciences invites applications and nominations for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor in the Health Informatics and Information Management (HIIM) program. This is a twelve-month faculty appointment in the fully online Master of Health Informatics and Information Management program. Faculty members also contribute to the education and mentorship of doctoral students in the Health Outcomes and Policy Research Program's Health Informatics and Information Management concentration. EDUCATION: Doctoral Degree in Health Informatics, Health Information Management, Management Information Systems, Business, Healthcare, or a closely related field. EXPERIENCE: Experience teaching analytics, artificial intelligence, health informatics, health information management, or data management. Knowledge of professional experience with healthcare information systems and computer applications in a healthcare environment. Excellent oral and written communication skills. DEPARTMENTAL PREFERENCES: Experience teaching at the college or university level. A sustained record of research, scholarship, and/or external funding. Experience with online teaching and distance education methodologies. Complete applications should include the following: Cover letter, updated Curriculum Vitae, name, and email of three professional references. References will not be contacted immediately. Applicants will be informed if/when references are contacted. Questions may be directed to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Marcia Sharp ( msharp10@uthsc.edu ). HEALTH INFORMATICS AND INFORMATION MANAGEMENT PROGRAM The Master of Health Informatics and Information Management (HIIM) program prepares graduate students to lead the management, analysis, and strategic use of health information across the healthcare continuum. The fully online program integrates health information management, health informatics, data analytics, artificial intelligence, information governance, healthcare technologies, leadership, and research to prepare graduates for leadership roles in healthcare, industry, and academia. Faculty are committed to excellence in teaching, scholarship, mentorship, and service while fostering an engaging online learning environment that emphasizes critical thinking, evidence-based practice, and innovation. In addition to educating master's students, program faculty contribute to the mentorship and education of doctoral students in the Health Outcomes and Policy Research Program's HIIM concentration. The program is housed within the Department of Diagnostic and Health Sciences in the College of Health Professions at the University of Tennessee Health Sciences. THE COLLEGE OF HEALTH PROFESSIONS The College of Health Professions is home to nationally recognized programs in allied health and rehabilitation sciences that prepare healthcare professionals through excellence in education, research, clinical practice, and community engagement. The college fosters interdisciplinary collaboration among its academic departments while supporting innovation, scholarship, and service to improve health outcomes locally and globally. THE UNIVERSITY OF TENNESSEE HEALTH SCIENCES The University of Tennessee Health Sciences is Tennessee's statewide academic health system and the flagship public academic health institution in the University of Tennessee System. Located in Memphis, UTHS includes six colleges—Health Professions, Dentistry, Graduate Health Sciences, Medicine, Nursing, and Pharmacy—and partners with leading clinical affiliates, including St. Jude Children's Research Hospital, Methodist Healthcare, Regional One Health, Le Bonheur Children's Hospital, Baptist Memorial Health Care, Memphis VA Medical Center, and St. Francis Hospital. The University of Tennessee Health Sciences is committed to excellence in education, research, clinical care, and community engagement. The university supports a robust research enterprise with approximately $85 million in annual sponsored funding from federal agencies, foundations, and industry partners. The University of Tennessee System serves more than 49,000 students, has over 360,000 living alumni, and an endowment exceeding $1 billion. Memphis boasts attractions, including Elvis Presley’s Graceland, the Memphis Grizzlies, historic Beale Street, the National Civil Rights Museum, the second-largest urban county park in the United States, and the Memphis in May World Championship Barbecue Cooking Contest. Develop, plan, and teach graduate courses assigned by the Program Director. Maintain an active program of scholarship, including research, grant development, professional presentations, peer-reviewed publications, and continuing education activities. Engage in service activities at the departmental, university, professional, and community levels, including committee participation and collaboration with faculty and professional colleagues. Recruit, advise, and mentor students to support their academic and professional success."
    },
    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/9094": {
      "title": "Instructor/ Assistant Professor of Dentistry - Knoxville, TN",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Knoxville, TN, United States THIS IS A NON-TENURE TRACK, PART-TIME 80% POSITION LOCATED IN KNOXVILLE, TN The University of Tennessee Health Sciences, Knoxville Dentistry seeks a part-time non-tenure track Instructor/Assistant Professor. Academic rank is based upon academic credentials. THIS IS A NON-TENURE TRACK, PART-TIME 80% POSITION LOCATED IN KNOXVILLE, TN The University of Tennessee Health Sciences, Knoxville Dentistry seeks a part-time non-tenure track Instructor/Assistant Professor. Academic rank is based upon academic credentials. EDUCATION: Completion of a General Practice Residency Program or Advanced Education in General Dentistry program required. EXPERIENCE: Previous teaching and supervisory experience preferred. Clinical experience in all areas of General Dentistry preferred. LICENSES: Tennessee Dental License required. Current DEA registration required. CPR and BCLS certificates are required. For benefits information, please visit https://www.uthsc.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefits-preview-packet.pdf THE UNIVERSITY OF TENNESSEE HEALTH SCIENCES, COLLEGE OF MEDICINE - KNOXVILLE The University of Tennessee College of Medicine – Knoxville (UT Health Sciences COM-Knoxville) was initially established in 1956 as the UT Memorial Research Center and Hospital, which also provided the graduate medical and dental educational (GMDE) and research programs in Knoxville. The GMDE programs collectively became the UT Graduate School of Medicine with the formation of the University of Tennessee Medical Center (UT Medical) in 1991, and more recently were renamed the UT Health Sciences COM-Knoxville with the increased emphasis on undergraduate medical education in Knoxville as well as the statewide presence of UT Health Sciences. The mission of the Knoxville Campus is to advance medical education required to train the next generation of physicians and dentists, deliver comprehensive and compassionate care with our hospital partner, UT Medical, and conduct innovative research that is meaningful for patients and their families. Our college provides training for third- and fourth-year Medical Students, second-year Physician Assistant Students, as well as Graduate Medical Education for 11 primary residency programs and 17 subspecialty fellowships. UT Health Sciences COM-Knoxville consists of 548 faculty (258 paid), 245 residents and fellows and hosts an average of 40-50 medical students per month. UT Health Sciences COM-Knoxville also provides Continuing Medical Education services for faculty, residents and practicing physicians in our region, as well as Advanced Medical Simulation for students, residents, and faculty. The UT Health Sciences College of Medicine-Knoxville, in partnership with UT Medical, sponsors extensive translational research in both clinical and laboratory settings. The faculty collaborates with various institutions both regionally and nationally including other UT Health Sciences campuses, UTK, Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL), and other health science center institutions. Helps residents develop presentations using photographs, PowerPoint, and other computer skills. Help develop and implement the program curriculum. Assists Program Director in the evaluation of resident training in affiliated institutions and off-service rotations. Provides clinical patient care as directed by the Program Director. Provides direct supervision of residents in patient care, including treatment planning, treatment, and follow-up care. Develops programs for resident instruction, to include lectures, seminars, and/or clinical demonstrations. Participates in educational activities of the department, including advisory board meetings, faculty meetings, journal club, and clinical competency committee meetings. Supervision of dental residents and staff, as assigned by the Program Director. Teaching residents, including lectures, mentorship, and/or supervision in the clinic and OR."
    },
    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/9097": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor - College of Dentistry",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Memphis, TN, United States The College of Dentistry at the University of Tennessee Health Science Center invites applications for a full-time non-tenured Open Rank Professor in the Department of Dental Hygiene. The College of Dentistry at the University of Tennessee Health Science Center invites applications for a full-time non-tenured Open Rank Professor in the Department of Dental Hygiene. EDUCATION: Bachelor’s Degree in Dental Hygiene from a Commission of Dental Accreditations (CODA) accredited Dental Hygiene program is required. (Master’s Degree in Dental Hygipreferred.) EXPERIENCE: Two (2) years of clinical practice experience as a Dental Hygienist. Familiarity with accreditation standards (CODA). Strong interpersonal, verbal and written communication, and organizational skills. Demonstrated commitment to student success and fostering an inclusive learning environment. Excellent computer skills and familiarity with technology to support effective teaching. LICENSES: Current Basic Life Support (BLS) certification. Current and unrestricted Dental Hygiene license in the State of Tennessee. Certified in local anesthesia and nitrous oxide administration in the State of Tennessee. DEPARTMENTAL PREFERENCES: Prior teaching or instructional experience in Dental Hygiene. Knowledge and experience in course design, development, and assessment. For benefits information, please visit https://www.uthsc.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefits-preview-packet.pdf THE UNIVERSITY OF TENNESSEE HEALTH SCIENCES The University of Tennessee Health Sciences is a statewide flagship, public, academic health institution in Tennessee. Founded in 1911, the mission of the University of Tennessee Health Sciences is to improve the health and well-being of Tennesseans and the global community by fostering collaborative education, research, scientific discovery, clinical care, and public service. Employing more than 4,600 people on its faculty, staff, and not-for-profit corporation faculty practice groups, and with more than 3,200 students across the state, UT Health Sciences contributes $4 billion to the economy of Tennessee. Part of the University of Tennessee System, the Health Sciences is headquartered in Memphis and includes all six of UT’s doctoral-degree-granting health science colleges -- Medicine, Dentistry, Pharmacy, Nursing, Graduate Health Sciences, and Health Professions. UT Health Sciences spans the state with its four major, regional clinical health science locations in Memphis, Knoxville, Chattanooga, and Nashville, as well as more than 100 clinical education sites across Tennessee. UT Health Sciences is the largest educator of health care professionals in the state and operates the state’s largest residency and fellowship advanced training programs. Located in West Tennessee on the banks of the Mississippi River, Memphis is the second-largest city in the state and among the largest cities in the Southeast. The Greater Memphis metropolitan area has more than 1.3 million residents, and the city ranks among those with the lowest cost of living in the country. It is home to a vibrant restaurant scene, a revitalized Downtown, the Midtown Arts District, many scenic neighborhoods, an active medical district, and a burgeoning airport in the midst of a $214 million modernization. Memphis boasts attractions, including Elvis Presley’s Graceland, the Memphis Grizzlies, historic Beale Street, the National Civil Rights Museum, the second-largest urban county park in the United States, and the Memphis in May World Championship Barbecue Cooking Contest. Provide instruction in clinical, didactic, and laboratory settings in accordance with curriculum and program standards. Develop and deliver comprehensive lesson plans and course materials that align with program outcomes. Evaluate and assess student performance through exams, projects, clinical evaluations, and various assessments. Stay up to date with advancements in dental hygiene practices and integrate new knowledge into teaching practices. Collaborate with faculty to enhance curriculum and refine teaching methodologies. Guide and support students through mentoring and academic advising. Participate in departmental meetings, engage in faculty development initiatives, and contribute to research, service, and patient care efforts. Participate in ongoing professional development and continuing education to stay up to date with advancements in the dental hygiene field. Engage in collaborative research projects with other faculty. Keep current with relevant literature to inform and integrate research into teaching and clinical practice."
    },
