    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/4835": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Memphis, TN, United States The University of Tennessee Health Science Center (UTHSC),Department of Anesthesiology, is seeking physician anesthesiologists for full-time academic faculty and clinician positions. The University of Tennessee Health Science Center (UTHSC),Department of Anesthesiology, is seeking physician anesthesiologists for full-time academic faculty and clinician positions. Individuals with fellowship training in the following Are strongly encouraged to apply: • Critical Care Medicine (CCM) • Regional Anesthesia (RA) • Chronic Pain Management (CP) • Obstetrical (OB) Anesthesia • Trauma Anesthesia Qualified generalists are also being sought. The patient population includes a heavy caseload in ortho, trauma, and high risk OB. The University of Tennessee Health Science Center (UTHSC),Department of Anesthesiology, is seeking physician anesthesiologists for full-time academic faculty and clinician positions. Individuals with fellowship training in the following Are strongly encouraged to apply: • Critical Care Medicine (CCM) • Regional Anesthesia (RA) • Chronic Pain Management (CP) • Obstetrical (OB) Anesthesia • Trauma Anesthesia Qualified generalists are also being sought. The patient population includes a heavy caseload in ortho, trauma, and high risk OB. Board certification or Board eligibility required. Completion of an accredited residency required and sub certifications/training highly preferred. A current unrestricted licensure as a Physician in Tennessee Current certification DEA number Eligible for malpractice insurance Relocation is not required, however the work is onsite. For benefits information, please visit https://www.uthsc.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefits-preview-packet.pdf Applicants should have a demonstrated commitment to and knowledge of equal employment opportunity and affirmative action. Tenure and non-tenure track positions are available. Duties include direct patient care as well as teaching and supervision of nurse anesthetists, students, fellows, and residents. Opportunities for clinical and basic science research are available and participation is encouraged. Academic rank is commensurate with training and experience and compensation is highly competitive. Eligible candidates should be board certified or eligible for examination by the ABA and eligible for licensure in the State of Tennessee. Interested individuals should send curriculum vitae, with names and addresses of three professional references, to Kelly Jeffrey, University of Tennessee Health Science Center, Department of Anesthesiology, 877 Jefferson Avenue, Suite 600, Memphis, TN38103, or by email to kjeffre4@uthsc.edu"
    },
