    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3743": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Radiology",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Memphis, TN, United States The University of Tennessee and Regional One Health are actively seeking applicants for a non-tenure-track academic clinical position of Assistant Professor in Radiology for work at Regional One Health, a Level I trauma center. The candidate will be a strong general radiologist with expertise in the specific area of breast imaging. The University of Tennessee and Regional One Health are actively seeking applicants for a non-tenure-track academic clinical position of Assistant Professor in Radiology for work at Regional One Health, a Level I trauma center. The candidate will be a strong general radiologist with expertise in the specific area of breast imaging. EDUCATION: Medical Doctor. Completion of an accredited residency required. Sub certifications/training in Breast Imaging required. LICENSES: Current unrestricted licensure as a Physician in Tennessee, Current certification DEA number. Eligible for malpractice insurance. Relocation is not required, however the work is on-site Interested candidates should send a letter of interest, two letters of recommendation, and a Curriculum Vitae to Harris L. Cohen, MD, Professor and Chair, University of Tennessee Health Science Center, Department of Radiology, 865 Jefferson, Suite Fl 50, Memphis, TN 31863 For benefits information, please visit https://www.uthsc.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefits-preview-packet.pdf THE UNIVERSITY OF TENNESSEE HEALTH SCIENCE CENTER The University of Tennessee Health Science Center is the flagship statewide, public, academic health institution in Tennessee. Founded in 1911, the mission of the University of Tennessee Health Science is to improve the health and well-being of Tennesseans and the global community by fostering integrated, collaborative, and inclusive education, research, scientific discovery, clinical care, and public service. Employing more than 4,600 people on its faculty, s