    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/1034": {
      "title": "Associate Professor-Physiology",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Memphis, TN, United States Candidates for this Tenure-track Associate Professor position are expected to have an active research program that complements existing departmental strengths in cardiovascular and renal diseases, diabetes, ion channel physiology, and mitochondrial biology. The qualified candidates should have an excellent record of research accomplishments and national funding The primary duties of this position are to maintain a vigorous, creative, externally funded research program, teach physiology to medical, dental, and graduate students, and provide service to the university and communities. This position comes with a competitive start-up package. The successful candidate will be in an outstanding position to take advantage of the exceptional opportunities and excellent resources available in the Department of Physiology, divisions of cardiology and nephrology, UTHSC campus, and local and statewide hospitals to develop collaborative research programs. Applicants must have a PhD, MD, or equivalent degree. The qualified candidates should have an excellent record of research accomplishments and national funding. To apply, applicants should submit a cover letter of interest, complete CV, summary of research accomplishments and goals, and names and contact information of three references. Please direct any questions to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Zheng Fan (zfan@uthsc.edu). The position will remain open until filled. The primary duties of this position are to perform cutting-edge research in the cardiovascular and renal field field, secure national funding, and teach physiology to medical, dental and graduate students. The Department of Physiology at the University of Tennessee Health Science Center (UTHSC) (https://www.uthsc.edu/physiology/) invites applications from and nominations of nationally-recognized individuals for a new tenure-track Associate Professor faculty position to build on its strengths in molecular and translational physiology research. The Department of Physiology at UTHSC was recently ranked in the top ten of all Physiology Departments in North America for total research funding. We seek candidates with an interest and demonstrated achievement in cardiovascular and renal research. We are particularly interested in candidates with an active research program that complements existing departmental strengths in cardiovascular diseases, diabetes, ion channel physiology, and mitochondrial biology. The primary duties of this position are to maintain a vigorous, creative, externally funded research program, teach physiology to medical, dental, and graduate students, and provide service to the university and communities. This position comes with a competitive start-up package. The successful candidate will be in an outstanding position to take advantage of the exceptional opportunities and excellent resources available in the Department of Physiology, divisions of cardiology and nephrology, UTHSC campus, and local and statewide hospitals to develop collaborative research programs."
    },
    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/2421": {
      "title": "Dermatology Open Rank Professor- College of Medicine",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Memphis, TN, United States The Kaplan-Amonette Department of Dermatology at the University of Tennessee Health Science Center in Memphis seeks a clinical dermatologist to join its growing faculty. This is a full-time or part-time, non-tenure track position. The Kaplan-Amonette Department of Dermatology at the University of Tennessee Health Science Center in Memphis seeks a clinical dermatologist to join its growing faculty. This is a full-time or part-time, non-tenure track position. Successful candidates must have an MD or DO degree and be eligible for full, unrestricted medical licensure in the state of Tennessee and be board certified in Dermatology. Rank and tenure will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Departmental Preferences: The successful candidate must have a solid clinical skill set and a commitment to the education of residents and medical students. THE UNIVERSITY OF TENNESSEE HEALTH SCIENCE CENTER The University of Tennessee Health Science Center is the flagship statewide, public, academic health institution in Tennessee. Founded in 1911, the mission of the University of Tennessee Health Science is to improve the health and well-being of Tennesseans and the global community by fostering integrated, collaborative, and inclusive education, research, scientific discovery, clinical care, and public service. Employing more than 4,600 people on its faculty, staff, and not-for-profit corporation faculty practice groups, and with more than 3,200 students across the state, UTHSC contributes $4 billion to the economy of Tennessee. Part of the University of Tennessee System, the Health Science Center is headquartered in Memphis and includes all six of UT’s doctoral-degree-granting health science colleges -- Medicine, Dentistry, Pharmacy, Nursing, Graduate Health Sciences, and Health Professions. UTHSC spans the state with its four major, regional clinical health science locations in Memphis, Knoxville, Chattanooga, and Nashville, as well as more than 100 clinical education sites across Tennessee. UTHSC is the largest educator of health care professionals in the state and operates the state’s largest residency and fellowship advanced training programs. Located in West Tennessee on the banks of the Mississippi River, Memphis is the second-largest city in the state and among the largest cities in the Southeast. The Greater Memphis metropolitan area has more than 1.3 million residents, and the city ranks among those with the lowest cost of living in the country. It is home to a vibrant restaurant scene, a revitalized Downtown, the Midtown Arts District, many scenic neighborhoods, an active medical district, and a burgeoning airport in the midst of a $214 million modernization. Memphis boasts attractions, including Elvis Presley’s Graceland, the Memphis Grizzlies, historic Beale Street, the National Civil Rights Museum, the second-largest urban county park in the United States, and the Memphis in May World Championship Barbecue Cooking Contest. The Kaplan-Amonette Department of Dermatology offers a full range of dermatological patient care with the opportunity to build your practice based on your particular interest. Our clinical program is strong and offers a range of services. The successful candidate must have a solid clinical skill set and a commitment to the education of residents and medical students. If desired, there is ample opportunity for clinical research and collaboration within the department as well as with other departments. The department is not only dynamically growing but also offers a collegial and supportive work environment for success."
    },
    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/2422": {
      "title": "Dermatology Open Rank Professor- College of Medicine",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Memphis, TN, United States The Kaplan-Amonette Department of Dermatology at the University of Tennessee Health Science Center in Memphis offers an outstanding opportunity for an academic pediatric dermatologist. This is a full-time, non-tenure-track position (rank to be determined by credentials and experience). The Kaplan-Amonette Department of Dermatology at the University of Tennessee Health Science Center in Memphis offers an outstanding opportunity for an academic pediatric dermatologist. This is a full-time, non-tenure-track position (rank to be determined by credentials and experience). Successful candidates must have an MD or DO degree and be eligible for full, unrestricted medical licensure in the state of Tennessee. Candidates must be board-certified/ board ­eligible and fellowship training in pediatric dermatology is required. Departmental Preferences: We seek a third pediatric dermatologist to help care for our large, diverse pediatric population. This position involves a joint appointment with the Department of Pediatrics. A candidate with an interest and/or expertise in the management of complex pediatric dermatologic diseases, as well as infectious diseases or skin diseases in immunosuppressed children, will be particularly attractive. THE UNIVERSITY OF TENNESSEE HEALTH SCIENCE CENTER The University of Tennessee Health Science Center is the flagship statewide, public, academic health institution in Tennessee. Founded in 1911, the mission of the University of Tennessee Health Science is to improve the health and well-being of Tennesseans and the global community by fostering integrated, collaborative, and inclusive education, research, scientific discovery, clinical care, and public service. Employing more than 4,600 people on its faculty, staff, and not-for-profit corporation faculty practice groups, and with more than 3,200 students across the state, UTHSC contributes $4 billion to the economy of Tennessee. Part of the University of Tennessee System, the Health Science Center is headquartered in Memphis and includes all six of UT’s doctoral-degree-granting health science colleges -- Medicine, Dentistry, Pharmacy, Nursing, Graduate Health Sciences, and Health Professions. UTHSC spans the state with its four major, regional clinical health science locations in Memphis, Knoxville, Chattanooga, and Nashville, as well as more than 100 clinical education sites across Tennessee. UTHSC is the largest educator of health care professionals in the state and operates the state’s largest residency and fellowship advanced training programs. Located in West Tennessee on the banks of the Mississippi River, Memphis is the second-largest city in the state and among the largest cities in the Southeast. The Greater Memphis metropolitan area has more than 1.3 million residents, and the city ranks among those with the lowest cost of living in the country. It is home to a vibrant restaurant scene, a revitalized Downtown, the Midtown Arts District, many scenic neighborhoods, an active medical district, and a burgeoning airport in the midst of a $214 million modernization. Memphis boasts attractions, including Elvis Presley’s Graceland, the Memphis Grizzlies, historic Beale Street, the National Civil Rights Museum, the second-largest urban county park in the United States, and the Memphis in May World Championship Barbecue Cooking Contest. With strong support from the University and our local dermatology community, the Department of Dermatology has grown at UTHSC. Our faculty now includes three academic dermatopathologists, five medical dermatologists, and two full time pediatric dermatologists. We seek a third pediatric dermatologist to help care for our large, diverse pediatric population. This position involves a joint appointment with the Department of Pediatrics, whose Chair, Dr. Jon McCullers. Clinical work will involve both outpatient and inpatient consultation services at Le Bonheur Children's Hospital and inpatient consultation privileges at St. Jude Children's Cancer Research Hospital. We serve a financially and ethnically diverse and often complicated patient population from Memphis and surrounding areas. Areas of research focus at Le Bonheur include pediatric obesity and asthma, and research opportunities there or at St. Jude with start-up funding may be available for the right candidate. We have a long-standing successful residency program (first established in 1967), and all faculty are active in resident and medical student education."
    },
    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/2423": {
      "title": "Emergency Medicine Assistant Professor- College of Medicine",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Memphis, TN, United States UT-Regional One Physicians, a partnership between Regional One Health and the University of Tennessee Health Science Center, seek full-time and/or part-time, non-tenure track Open Academic Rank / Physician who will provide care in the Emergency Medicine Department located in downtown Memphis. This position is intended for clinical faculty with an effort in teaching, leadership, innovation and clinical service in Emergency Medicine. The specific instructional role is flexible and will include a combination of direct teaching, emergency medicine services, resident advising, assessment of resident performance, research and other roles as determined by the developing needs of the College of Medicine. Compensation is consistent with private emergency medicine services in the region. UT-Regional One Physicians, a partnership between Regional One Health and the University of Tennessee Health Science Center, seek full-time and/or part-time, non-tenure track Open Academic Rank / Physician who will provide care in the Emergency Medicine Department located in downtown Memphis. This position is intended for clinical faculty with an effort in teaching, leadership, innovation and clinical service in Emergency Medicine. The specific instructional role is flexible and will include a combination of direct teaching, emergency medicine services, resident advising, assessment of resident performance, research and other roles as determined by the developing needs of the College of Medicine. Compensation is consistent with private emergency medicine services in the region. Board certification or Board eligible in Emergency Medicine required. Completion of an accredited residency required and sub certifications/training highly preferred. Current unrestricted licensure as a Physician in Tennessee. Current certification DEA number. Eligible for malpractice insurance. THE UNIVERSITY OF TENNESSEE HEALTH SCIENCE CENTER The University of Tennessee Health Science Center is the flagship statewide, public, academic health institution in Tennessee. Founded in 1911, the mission of the University of Tennessee Health Science is to improve the health and well-being of Tennesseans and the global community by fostering integrated, collaborative, and inclusive education, research, scientific discovery, clinical care, and public service. Employing more than 4,600 people on its faculty, staff, and not-for-profit corporation faculty practice groups, and with more than 3,200 students across the state, UTHSC contributes $4 billion to the economy of Tennessee. Part of the University of Tennessee System, the Health Science Center is headquartered in Memphis and includes all six of UT’s doctoral-degree-granting health science colleges -- Medicine, Dentistry, Pharmacy, Nursing, Graduate Health Sciences, and Health Professions. UTHSC spans the state with its four major, regional clinical health science locations in Memphis, Knoxville, Chattanooga, and Nashville, as well as more than 100 clinical education sites across Tennessee. UTHSC is the largest educator of health care professionals in the state and operates the state’s largest residency and fellowship advanced training programs. Located in West Tennessee on the banks of the Mississippi River, Memphis is the second-largest city in the state and among the largest cities in the Southeast. The Greater Memphis metropolitan area has more than 1.3 million residents, and the city ranks among those with the lowest cost of living in the country. It is home to a vibrant restaurant scene, a revitalized Downtown, the Midtown Arts District, many scenic neighborhoods, an active medical district, and a burgeoning airport in the midst of a $214 million modernization. Memphis boasts attractions, including Elvis Presley’s Graceland, the Memphis Grizzlies, historic Beale Street, the National Civil Rights Museum, the second-largest urban county park in the United States, and the Memphis in May World Championship Barbecue Cooking Contest. This position is intended for clinical faculty with an effort in teaching, leadership, innovation and clinical service in Emergency Medicine. The specific instructional role is flexible and will include a combination of direct teaching, emergency medicine services, resident advising, assessment of resident performance, research and other roles as determined by the developing needs of the College of Medicine. Compensation is consistent with private emergency medicine services in the region. Working with Regional One Health, the University of Tennessee has established the only emergency residency program in Western Tennessee. The hospital’s emergency department is being designed as a model for high throughput emergency care in a facility with the only level I trauma center in the region. The program we seek to develop includes clinical experience in a highly structured environment, residency teaching with very qualified emergency medicine house staff and research that will extend to multiple areas (stroke, wound care, ultrasound, etc). Our goal is to transform the emergency medicine physician workforce in Western Tennessee to the benefits of our communities/patients and trainees. This is an important priority for both the medical school and health system."
    },
    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/2412": {
