ing on the senior leadership team of the Department. The role will involve recruitment, retention, mentoring, and career development of other faculty members and trainees. The successful candidate will demonstrate clinical skills in pediatrics or a pediatric subspecialty and a history of working with a culturally diverse pediatric population. The position involves education of trainees at all levels in the individual’s sub-specialty. A personal research program will be encouraged."
